+# IndoHiTAB / HiTAB annotation app — schema and workflow v3
+
+**Scope:** This change set is based on the previous `hitab_feature_work` application, **not** on any later code edits on your Mac. Merge rather than overwrite local changes. The uploaded `upload_hitab_v2.zip` is source data and is **not included in the public source package**.
+
+## 0. Before any production migration
+
+1. Commit your current Mac source, back up your Supabase database (including `tqa_tables`, `table_cells`, `qa_pairs`, `table_reviews`, `qa_reviews`, `profiles`, `user_roles`). Test on a disposable Supabase project first. Do not repeat old migrations.
+2. Verify `public.table_reviews` and `public.qa_reviews` exist. This migration depends on `20260918090000_add_validator_reviews.sql` (previous validator patch) and on its `review_queue` functions.
+3. Audit the current schema for manual changes since the last ZIP; reconcile incompatible names/columns before applying this migration.
+4. Run **only** `supabase/migrations/20260918110000_preserve_hitab_sampling_audit.sql` in Supabase SQL Editor as a single query. SQL has not been executed against your actual Supabase instance here.
+5. Update the web source code as well. Old clients send `status`, `updated_by` and `updated_at` directly and will be rejected by the new column permissions.
+
+## 1. Fields and rules
+
+| Table | Fields added | Behavior |
+|---|---|---|
+| `tqa_tables` | `original_table_id` TEXT, `original_table`, `annotated_table`, `validated_table` JSONB, `annotate_flag` INTEGER | Original write-once; annotated is derived from original matrix plus translated title/cells; validated from review output. Flag=1 by default. |
+| `qa_pairs` | `original_question_id` TEXT, `original_qa`, `annotated_qa`, `validated_qa` JSONB, `dataset_split`, `annotate_flag` | Original typed `answer` array, `aggregation`, `linked_cells`, `answer_formulas` and `reference_cells_map` are preserved in each snapshot. New Indonesian question/answer text is stored separately under `question_id`/`answer_id`; no automated rewriting of numeric answers or formulas. Flag=1 by default. |
+| `table_cells` | `row_index`, `column_index` | Zero-based coordinates; NULL on legacy rows until real coordinates are imported. Never infer from `position`. |
+| `qa_reviews` | `logic_confirmed` BOOLEAN | Required to complete a review when `original_qa` is present. This is a human confirmation, **not** an automated correctness guarantee. |
+| `user_work_log` | actor, role, item and original IDs, action, timestamp, before/after JSON | Server-derived immutable append-only events. A work item opening produces `opened`; changing a translation or review produces `saved`, `completed` or `reopened`. Admin can see all records; each signed-in user can see their own. |
+
+**Independent sampling:** `tqa_tables.annotate_flag=0` removes table translation/review. `qa_pairs.annotate_flag=0` removes QA translation/review. An independently sampled QA may still appear when its parent table is not sampled. Both existing and newly inserted records start at **1**; changing a flag does not destroy previous translations or review data.
+
+**Original records:** Historical rows with no genuine source JSON remain `original_table=NULL` or `original_qa=NULL`. The migration never manufactures original metadata from translation text; such rows need a deliberate, ID-matched backfill.
+
+## 2. Where to change your Mac code
+
+| File | Role |
+|---|---|
+| `supabase/migrations/20260918110000_preserve_hitab_sampling_audit.sql` | Additive schema, write-once original guards, source/translated/reviewed snapshots, logging, sampling guards, reviewer queues, atomic save RPC, server progress RPCs, RLS/column permissions. |
+| `src/routes/_authenticated/terjemahan.$tableId.tsx` | Original + annotated matrix preview, original QA reasoning, sampled QA filter, atomic save, work-open event. |
+| `src/routes/_authenticated/terjemahan.index.tsx` | Display tables with sampled tables **or** sampled QA. |
+| `src/routes/_authenticated/pemeriksaan.$jenis.$id.tsx` | Show source table + QA reasoning, require explicit QA logic review, work-open event. |
+| `src/routes/_authenticated/pengguna.tsx` | Admin controls independent flags by **original ID** and inspects latest 100 work events (filter by user). |
+| `src/routes/_authenticated/dasbor.tsx` | Accurate sampled counts via database RPC; avoids Supabase's normal 1,000-row REST cap. |
+| `src/components/HiTabTablePreview.tsx`, `src/components/HiTabQaLogic.tsx` | Render real matrix/merged cells and read-only formula/linked-cell evidence. |
+| `src/hooks/useWorkOpen.ts` | One opening event per selected item, only after authorization/readiness. |
+| `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts` | Updated Supabase TS typing; regenerate from your **actual schema** if different. |
+| `scripts/import_hitab.py` | Offline dry-run and optional insert-only import from a local original ZIP. |
+
+## 3. Inspect the supplied dataset ZIP (offline first)
+
+From the project root on your Mac (replace the ZIP path with its real location):
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/import_hitab.py ~/Downloads/upload_hitab_v2.zip
+python3 scripts/import_hitab.py ~/Downloads/upload_hitab_v2.zip --limit-tables 5
+```
+
+The actual uploaded ZIP contains **2,997 table JSON files** and **6,390 QA rows** across train/test. **269 QA rows refer to 113 table IDs not present in the archive**; the importer reports and skips these, without inventing a parent table. A full import would prepare **6,121 QA rows** and **114,780 nonempty header/row-label cells**. It does not translate ordinary numeric/body values. If you need those translated too, adapt `prepare_cells` deliberately and re-evaluate annotation workload.
+
+`--limit-tables 5` is a useful initial test **on a fresh database**. The script is insert-only with deterministic UUIDs and does not reset source records or re-import overwritten translations. If you already imported the data another way and have different UUIDs, do **not** run the script blindly: reconcile original IDs to existing UUIDs first.
+
+**Optional production import** (do not run until the migration is confirmed and you understand costs, missing data and duplicates):
+
+```bash
+export SUPABASE_URL='https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co'
+export SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY='YOUR_SECRET_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY'
+python3 scripts/import_hitab.py ~/Downloads/upload_hitab_v2.zip --limit-tables 5 --apply
+unset SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
+```
+
+The service-role key must stay in your local shell/server and is **never** a `VITE_*` variable or a value in published code. Consider using a separate terminal session with no shared screen or recorded commands for secrets. Once testing is complete, omit `--limit-tables` only if you deliberately want the full available source import.
+
+## 4. Check the data after migration/import
+
+```sql
+-- All initial sampling flags are 1, unless you manually changed some.
+SELECT annotate_flag, count(*) FROM public.tqa_tables GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1;
+SELECT annotate_flag, count(*) FROM public.qa_pairs GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1;
+
+-- Original IDs are independent of internal UUIDs.
+SELECT id, original_table_id, original_table IS NOT NULL AS has_source,
+       annotated_table IS NOT NULL AS has_translation
+FROM public.tqa_tables LIMIT 10;
+SELECT id, original_question_id, dataset_split,original_qa->'answer' AS original_answer,
+       original_qa->'aggregation' AS original_logic
+FROM public.qa_pairs WHERE original_qa IS NOT NULL LIMIT 10;
+
+-- Before/after/final snapshots for a chosen source ID.
+SELECT original_table,annotated_table,validated_table
+FROM public.tqa_tables WHERE original_table_id='REPLACE_WITH_REAL_TABLE_ID';
+SELECT original_qa,annotated_qa,validated_qa
+FROM public.qa_pairs WHERE original_question_id='REPLACE_WITH_REAL_QA_ID';
+
+-- All audit events, read in SQL Editor / admin only.
+SELECT occurred_at,actor_id,actor_role,item_type,source_table_id,source_question_id,
+       action,before_value,after_value
+FROM public.user_work_log ORDER BY occurred_at DESC LIMIT 30;
+```
+
+Sampling can be edited in the app under **Pengguna → Sampling anotasi**. Use the *original filename stem* as table ID, and `id` from JSONL as the QA ID. Never confuse QA `question_id` (Indonesian translation TEXT field in legacy schema) with `original_question_id` (source record ID).
+
+## 5. Validation checks before public release
+
+- Sign in as an annotator, open an eligible table/QA, save, and confirm `user_work_log` identifies the actual user and before/after values, `annotated_table` changes but `original_table` does not.
+- Sign in as a validator: translation not ready or flag 0 must block; review drafts must persist; final QA review with source JSON requires `logic_confirmed=true`; a later translator correction must reopen the review and clear the final snapshot.
+- Sign in as admin, set **table=0, QA=1** for a QA whose parent is excluded: only QA editing/review should be available.
+- Try to change `original_table` or `original_qa` from a normal authenticated client: the operation must fail; check anonymous client cannot read work logs.
+- Verify complete original hierarchy, merged cells, typed answers and formula references against a few real JSON records.
+- Check `git status` and `git diff --cached --name-only` before publishing. Never commit original ZIP, `.env.local`, Supabase service-role key, user emails, or private/uncleared dataset data. Review third-party dataset license terms separately from the code license.
+
+**Testing limit:** Python importer unit tests and TypeScript syntax checks were run locally. We do not have access to your Supabase database, and a PostgreSQL migration/integration test and complete `npm run build` have not been executed here. Validate on staging before applying to production or claiming production readiness.
