+# IndoHiTAB annotation platform — v4 roles & work assignment
+
+This package is **cumulative**: it includes the earlier Validator patch, v3 original/annotated/validated JSON snapshots, sampling flags, activity audit log, and this v4 explicit role/work assignment change.
+
+## What changed in v4
+
+1. **Registration no longer auto-assigns Anotator.** `handle_new_user()` creates only a `profiles` row with `status='menunggu_peran'`. An Admin must explicitly assign `Anotator`, `Validator`, or `Admin`.
+2. **User & role menu.** `/pengguna` now supports `Belum ditetapkan` and uses an atomic Admin-only database function to change roles.
+3. **Work assignment menu.** `/penugasan` lets Admin assign an active Anotator and Validator independently to each sampled (or unsampled) table/QA using the original HiTAB table/question ID.
+4. **Assignment enforcement.** Anotators can write only assigned tables/QA. Validators can review only assigned tables/QA. Admin can override.
+5. **Existing v3 sampling remains independent.** `annotate_flag` is not changed by assignment. Assignment and sampling are separate controls.
+6. **Existing audit log remains active.** Open/save/complete/reopen events still identify the actor. The assignment columns identify who is responsible for the item.
+
+## Database migration order
+
+If you already installed the previous patches, run **only** the new migration:
+
+```text
+supabase/migrations/20260918130000_roles_and_work_assignment.sql
+```
+
+It expects these earlier migrations to already exist:
+
+```text
+20260918090000_add_validator_reviews.sql
+20260918110000_preserve_hitab_sampling_audit.sql
+```
+
+Back up the database and test in staging first.
+
+### Important behavior after migration
+
+Existing users keep their current role. Existing users who have **no** `user_roles` row are marked `menunggu_peran`.
+
+Existing `tqa_tables.assigned_to` values are copied to `tqa_tables.annotator_id` when available. Otherwise work is initially unassigned. QA rows are initially unassigned unless you assign them in `/penugasan`.
+
+This is deliberate: the migration does **not** guess who should validate or annotate each QA.
+
+## Installing the cumulative patch on the original uploaded project
+
+The cumulative patch is built against the original `hiTab-tqa-proyek.zip` state and includes the previous Validator + v3 changes.
+
+```bash
+cd ~/Downloads/hiTab-tqa-proyek
+git status
+git apply --check ~/Downloads/hitab_v4_cumulative.patch
+```
+
+If there is no error:
+
+```bash
+git apply ~/Downloads/hitab_v4_cumulative.patch
+```
+
+If `git apply --check` fails, do not force it. Your Mac source differs from the uploaded baseline; merge the changed files instead.
+
+## Recommended workflow
+
+1. User registers and confirms email.
+2. Admin opens **Pengguna & Peran** and assigns Anotator or Validator.
+3. Admin opens **Penugasan** and chooses a table or QA assignment.
+4. Sampling remains controlled separately with `annotate_flag` (`1` = included, `0` = excluded).
+5. Anotator sees only assigned work in Penerjemahan.
+6. Validator sees only assigned work in Pemeriksaan.
+7. Admin can inspect `user_work_log` for who opened/saved/completed work.
+
+## Files added/changed
+
+- `supabase/migrations/20260918130000_roles_and_work_assignment.sql`
+- `src/routes/_authenticated/pengguna.tsx`
+- `src/routes/_authenticated/penugasan.tsx`
+- `src/components/AppShell.tsx`
+- `src/routes/index.tsx`
+- `src/routes/_authenticated/terjemahan.index.tsx`
+- `src/routes/_authenticated/terjemahan.$tableId.tsx`
+- `src/routes/_authenticated/pemeriksaan.$jenis.$id.tsx`
+- `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts`
+- `src/routeTree.gen.ts`
+
+After applying the real Supabase migration, regenerate `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts` from your live schema if possible; the checked-in type file is a convenience snapshot, not a substitute for schema generation.
